        "subject": "LU-20300 ldiskfs: add series for Ubuntu 26.04 7.0.0-40",
        "message": "LU-20300 ldiskfs: add series for Ubuntu 26.04 7.0.0-40\n\nThe ldiskfs build fails on Ubuntu 26.04 kernel 7.0.0-43-generic:\n\n  Applying patch patches/linux-6.12/ext4-filename-encode.patch\n  1 out of 12 hunks FAILED\n\nUbuntu 7.0.0-40 picked up two upstream ext4 changes.  One adds an\next4_hash_in_dirent() bounds check to the condition in\next4_search_dir() that ext4-filename-encode.patch rewrites.  The\nother adds EXT4_IGET_NOWAIT (0x0010) to ext4_iget_flags, which\nboth breaks the context of ext4-add-IGET_NO_CHECKS-flag.patch and\ntakes the value it used for EXT4_IGET_NO_CHECKS.\n\nAdd ubuntu26.04 versions of the two patches, with\nEXT4_IGET_NO_CHECKS moved to 0x0020, and a 7.0.0-40-ubuntu26\nseries that uses them.  Select it for patch level 40 and later.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I7a6b6388cd220078db31ac3df32d48156a6a6964\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70770\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: James Simmons <jsimmons@infradead.org>\nReviewed-by: Minh <mdiep@thelustrecollective.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
